{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.a3_target_fragile_but_sign_robust","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.a3_target_fragile_but_sign_robust","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L102-L112","doc":"**Capstone.** The A=3 magnitude target is a small residual (`μ₃ = M3` exactly, `mu3_eq_M3`) whose\nrelative sensitivity to the subtracted baseline exceeds unity (`residual_amplifies`) — numerically `>7`\n(`corpus_amplification_gt_seven`) — so its magnitude is baseline-class-relative\n(`spread_exceeds_gap`), while its sign is robust (`mu3_positive_all_baselines`,\n`mu4_negative_all_baselines`). scope-(a): a fragility/robustness structure, NOT a magnitude derivation\nand NOT a refutation of the principled graded-dimension baseline; nothing wired. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.residual_framing_gt_36_pct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.residual_framing_gt_36_pct","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L98-L100","doc":"**The residual framing is large** (`Δ/μ₃ > 36%`, model reaches `0.63·μ₃`) — the same miss, `≈8×`\nmagnified by the small-residual denominator (`physical_miss_lt_five_pct` vs this). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.physical_miss_lt_five_pct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.physical_miss_lt_five_pct","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L94-L96","doc":"**Physical accuracy is modest.** At the corpus values the miss on the physical ratio\n`B(³H)/B(²H)` is `Δ/ρ = 0.1737689/3.8128 < 5%` — the frame-independent A=3 accuracy statement. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.framing_amplification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.framing_amplification","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L85-L92","doc":"**Framing amplification identity.** The single absolute miss `Δ` of the model against the physical\nratio, expressed as a fraction of the small residual `μ` (the \"1.6× gap\") versus the full physical ratio\n`ρ` (the frame-independent accuracy), differ by exactly the factor `ρ/μ`:\n`(Δ/μ) / (Δ/ρ) = ρ/μ`. The alarming multiplicative gap is the modest physical miss magnified by\n`ρ/μ ≈ 8`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.spread_exceeds_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.spread_exceeds_gap","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L78-L82","doc":"**The μ₃ baseline-class spread exceeds the gap it targets.** The magnitude spread\n`μ₃^max / μ₃^min = 0.8128 / 0.4708 ≈ 1.73` exceeds the `1.585×` gap the closure attempts aim to close\n(`0.8128 > 1.585 · 0.4708`). Hence the target's own convention-spread is larger than the gap:\nthe \"1.6× A=3 magnitude gap\" is baseline-CLASS-relative, not absolute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.mu4_negative_all_baselines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.mu4_negative_all_baselines","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L72-L76","doc":"**μ₄ sign is robust** (negative) across the three baselines — reported μ₄ values\n`−4.591, −2.554, −2.220`. Together with `mu3_positive_all_baselines`, the SIGN structure\n(μ₃>0, μ₄<0) survives the baseline change even though the magnitudes do not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.mu3_positive_all_baselines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.mu3_positive_all_baselines","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L67-L70","doc":"**μ₃ sign is robust** (positive) across the three deuteron-normalized A-scaling baselines\nG (graded), Q (quantum), C (classical) — reported μ₃ values `0.4708, 0.7691, 0.8128`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.corpus_amplification_gt_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.corpus_amplification_gt_seven","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L62-L65","doc":"**Corpus amplification `> 7`.** At the reported corpus values `ρ_grad(3) ≈ 3.342031`,\n`μ₃ ≈ 0.4708`, the amplification `ρ_grad(3)/μ₃ > 7`: a 1% error in the subtracted baseline moves μ₃ by\nmore than 7%. (Consumes the witness numbers; an arithmetic fact about the reported target.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.residual_amplifies","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.residual_amplifies","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L55-L60","doc":"**Relative amplification exceeds unity when the residual is smaller than its baseline.**\nIf the residual `r = S − G` satisfies `0 < r < G`, then `1 < G / r`: a *relative* baseline error is\nmagnified by the factor `G/r > 1` in the residual. (`resid_shift` gives the absolute unit gain; this\nconverts it to the relative gain `G/r`.) For μ₃ this is `ρ_grad(3)/μ₃ ≈ 7`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.resid_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.resid_shift","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L49-L53","doc":"**The residual moves by exactly the baseline shift** (unit absolute gain, opposite sign):\nshifting `ρ_grad ↦ ρ_grad + d` moves the residual by `−d`. There is no attenuation — every bit of\nbaseline error passes straight into the target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.mu3_eq_M3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.mu3_eq_M3","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L41-L46","doc":"**The simplex re-expression adds no robustness.** With the deuteron self-reference forcing\n`μ₂ = M(2) = 0`, the 3-body simplex coefficient `μ₃ = M3 − 3·μ₂` equals the raw A=3 residual `M3`\n*exactly* — so μ₃ inherits ALL of the residual's baseline sensitivity; expanding in the simplex basis\ndoes not stabilize the target. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.resid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.Mu3BaselineFragility.resid","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/Mu3BaselineFragility.lean#L36-L38","doc":"The graded-subtracted residual as a function of the subtracted baseline `G`\n(the strong ratio `S = ρ_strong(A)` is fixed data): `resid S G = S − G`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}